1. INITIAL GIT SETUP & CONFIGURATION
================================================================================
Run these once when setting up Git on your machine.

# Set your name (appears in commit logs)
git config --global user.name "Your Name"

# Set your email (must match your GitHub account email)
git config --global user.email "your.email@example.com"

# Set default branch name to 'main'
git config --global init.defaultBranch main

# Verify your settings
git config --list


================================================================================
2. STARTING A PROJECT
================================================================================

--- Option A: You are starting a brand new local project ---
# 1. Initialize Git in your project folder
git init

# 2. Add files to staging
git add .

# 3. Create initial commit
git commit -m "feat: initial commit"

# 4. Link local repository to GitHub
git remote add origin https://github.com/username/repository-name.git

# 5. Push local code to GitHub main branch
git push -u origin main


--- Option B: Joining an existing team project ---
# Clone the remote repository to your local machine
git clone https://github.com/username/repository-name.git

# Navigate into the project folder
cd repository-name


