6. UNDOING MISTAKES & REVERTING CHANGES
================================================================================

# Unstage a file (keep local changes)
git restore --staged filename.js

# Discard all uncommitted local changes in a file (DESTRUCTIVE)
git restore filename.js

# Discard ALL uncommitted changes in the entire working directory (DESTRUCTIVE)
git reset --hard

# Change the last commit message (before pushing)
git commit --amend -m "feat: updated commit message"

# Undo the last commit, but KEEP your changes staged
git reset --soft HEAD~1

# Safely undo a commit that was already pushed to GitHub (creates a new undo commit)
git revert <commit-hash>


