7. RESOLVING MERGE CONFLICTS STEP-BY-STEP
================================================================================
Merge conflicts happen when two people edit the same lines in the same file.

1. When git merge or git pull fails with a conflict:
   git status  (Shows conflicting files under "Unmerged paths")

2. Open conflicting files in VS Code / IDE. Look for conflict markers:
   <<<<<<< HEAD (Your current branch changes)
   Your code...
   =======
   Teammate's code...
   >>>>>>> origin/main (Incoming changes)

3. Edit the file to keep the correct code and remove conflict markers.

4. Stage the resolved files:
   git add filename.js

5. Complete the merge commit:
   git commit -m "fix: resolve merge conflict between main and feature branch"

6. Push the updated code:
   git push origin feature/add-login-page


